threads.body:
Please don't special-case `response`. With absent and null being equivalent, `None` can be dropped here too. Semconv making `response` optional is in open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-genai#688.

```suggestion
        dumped = {f.name: getattr(value, f.name) for f in fields(value)}
        if type(value).__module__ == _GENAI_TYPES_MODULE:
            # None means "not set" in util-genai types. User dataclasses, such
            # as those inside tool payloads, keep their None values.
            dumped = {k: v for k, v in dumped.items() if v is not None}
```

The `ToolCallResponsePart` import and `test_tool_response_keeps_none` would go as well.

